ok   rate_limit declarations are registered in order
ok   a declaration keeps its by:, with:, if:, unless:, name: and store:
ok   requests under the limit pass; the next is a 429 with Retry-After
ok   only: leaves the other actions alone
ok   the window closing resets the count
ok   behind a trusted proxy each forwarded address has its own count
ok   without a trusted proxy X-Forwarded-For is ignored
ok   by: :remote_addr counts the peer even behind a trusted proxy
ok   redirect_to: answers a 303 with the alert in the flash
ok   a limit inherited from a parent counts each controller apart
ok   hit answers 0 while allowed and the seconds left once exhausted
ok   a full table drops the oldest windows first
ok   a full table drops every expired window before an open one
ok   a window that reopens moves its key to the back of the table
ok   the table never holds more than max_keys keys
ok   rate_limit refuses a bad to:, within:, store: or name:
ok   current_time follows the clock: real time, then a travel
ok   Retry-After is the rest of the aligned window
ok   the cache key is rate-limit:<controller_path>:<name>:<key>:<window>
ok   store: :memory keeps the per-process counter
ok   reset_all! forgets the counts in the cache too
ok   by: a method keys the count by its value
ok   by: a method that answers an empty key is an error, not one bucket for everyone
ok   with: answers instead of 429
ok   a with: method that renders nothing is followed by the 429
ok   if: false skips the limit; unless: true skips it
ok   two limits with name: on one action count apart
ok   a cache-store limit inherited from a parent counts each controller apart
